  "body": {
    "id": "prop:mechanism-cluster-count",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Let \\(C_B,C_{CR}>0\\) be cluster budgets for the optimized Bernoulli-label and exact-count designs.  If the Bernoulli design is required to have no larger leading local simple regret than the exact-count design, namely\n\\[\n\\frac{R_{B,A}^\\star(v_A)}{\\sqrt{C_B}}\n\\leq\n\\frac{R_{CR,A}^\\star(v_A)}{\\sqrt{C_{CR}}},\n\\]\nthen\n\\[\n\\frac{C_B}{C_{CR}}\n\\geq\n\\left\\{\\frac{R_{B,A}^\\star(v_A)}{R_{CR,A}^\\star(v_A)}\\right\\}^{2}\n\\geq\\frac1{s_{A,\\max}}\n\\geq\\frac1{1-2^{1-n}}.\n\\]\nEquality in the mechanism inequality \\(\\{R_{B,A}^\\star/R_{CR,A}^\\star\\}^2\\geq1/s_{A,\\max}\\) holds exactly under the support-and-normalized-active-vector criterion in \\(\\texttt{thm:mechanism-loss}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "C_B",
      "C_{CR}",
      "R_{B,A}^\\star",
      "R_{CR,A}^\\star",
      "v_A",
      "s_{A,\\max}",
      "n"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:mechanism-loss"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "All mechanism values are positive by \\(\\texttt{thm:mechanism-loss}\\).  Squaring the assumed leading-regret comparison and rearranging gives\n\\[\n\\frac{C_B}{C_{CR}}\\geq\n\\left\\{\\frac{R_{B,A}^\\star}{R_{CR,A}^\\star}\\right\\}^{2}. \\tag{46}\n\\]\nSquaring the mechanism bound gives the next inequality and preserves its equality criterion.  Convexity of \\(x\\mapsto x^n\\) gives, for \\(x\\in[0,1]\\),\n\\[\nx^n+(1-x)^n\\geq2(1/2)^n=2^{1-n}. \\tag{47}\n\\]\nEvery active target count is strictly between zero and \\(n\\), so for column \\(\\ell\\),\n\\[\n\\sum_{k\\in A}B_{k\\ell}\n\\leq1-\\pi_\\ell^n-(1-\\pi_\\ell)^n\\leq1-2^{1-n}. \\tag{48}\n\\]\nMaximizing over \\(\\ell\\) gives \\(s_{A,\\max}\\leq1-2^{1-n}\\).  Reciprocation is valid because the quantities are positive, and (46)--(48) prove the result.\n",
    "justification": "The squared local-regret frontier is the prospective cluster-count penalty.",
    "gap": "The mechanism theorem's risk frontier needs an explicit prospective sample-size implication.",
    "consumer": "It translates the mechanism deficiency into a sample-size lower bound.",
